From 2a9d3540740ebdfa5b918236d3457bce4945dcf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: cli: git: add raw ref push command

Code review systems and other Git applications accept commits through
application-specific refs such as `refs/for/main`

Add `jj git ref push` to send one revision to a fully qualified ref on a
named remote without creating or tracking a bookmark

Require one explicit update policy: `--force`, `--expected-at`, or
`--expected-absent`. This prevents the command from defaulting to an
unguarded update

This plumbing command pushes the selected Git commit as stored. It skips
the eligibility checks and `git.sign-on-push` behavior of `jj git push`

Closes #4388

